WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.557 --> 00:00:02.350
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.510
- [Wasim] Pilgrims come
from all over the world

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.790
to get tattooed in the Holy
Land from the old stamps.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.200
Some of those stamps are
older than the United States,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.260
and they were passed down in my family

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.590
from one generation to another.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.070
I am Wasim Razzouk, and
I am the 27th generation

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.878
of the oldest tattooing
family in the world.

00:00:21.878 --> 00:00:24.290
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.530
- [Announcer] This Great Big Story

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.253
is inspired by Genesis.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.340
- The cross tattoo on the
wrist is the ultimate proof

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.120
of pilgrimage to the Holy Land.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.320
They are now reborn Christians;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.470
they are proud of their
journey that they have done.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:48.360
When they understand the
history and our lineage,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.020
they wanna be tattooed by us.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.180
I learned tattooing from my father,

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.930
who learned it from his father.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:56.423
My son is the 28th generation.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.610
My family were doing tattoos in Egypt

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.080
just like mine here, a small,
little cross on the wrist.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.820
When they came to the
Holy Land, 500 years ago,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.830
they discovered a
tradition where Christians

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:12.360
would get a tattoo as a
mark of the pilgrimage.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.450
So my family decided to stay here

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.423
and continue this tradition.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.730
Your stamp is 500 years old, guaranteed.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:21.563
- All right, okay.

00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:22.720
- Okay.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.810
Among the tools that we have in the family

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:30.270
that has been passed down are
beautiful, old, wooden stamps

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.020
that are hundreds of years old.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.590
And those stamps are very
simple, just outlined designs,

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.350
but very intricate, and very charming,

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.400
and that's why a lot of people like them.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.820
We get people from all
over the world who come

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.090
to get a tattoo out of a old, wooden stamp

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.630
that has touched so many pilgrims

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:53.310
who have done the same
journey that they are doing;

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.270
so they are becoming part of this history,

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.770
part of this tradition,
and part of this heritage.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.080
What we're doing here is
not a cosmetic tattoo;

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.200
it's a tattoo that has
way more deeper meaning

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.470
than the superficial skin.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.580
They're actually reflecting
what they have felt

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.260
when they came to the Holy Land,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.770
and now they want to
reflect that on their skin.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.140
It's almost like baptism;

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.140
it's almost like baptizing somebody,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.850
and that's a big responsibility.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:28.010
At the same time it's greatly satisfying

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.150
to feel that you are that special person,

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.890
that they want you to tattoo them.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:37.120
It's for the tradition;
it's for that special thing

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.080
in their life that has happened to them

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.718
that they want to be marked by you.

00:02:41.718 --> 00:02:44.301
(light music)

